  "simplifications": [
    "One step = one engine iteration; a prompt is prefilled in one step (no chunked prefill, no token budget).",
    "No prefix caching in this comparison; a preempted paged request recomputes its prompt and outputs.",
    "Contiguous policies never preempt because they reserve memory up front.",
    "Memory categories: token_states = KV slots already written; reserved_future = reserved slots that will be written later; internal_fragmentation = allocated slots never written (paged: last-block slack); external_fragmentation = free slots on a step where the next request is blocked although enough total memory is free; unallocated = other free slots."
  ]
